y of the other curse spirit  being things that appeared alongside mr  happy face because the cyclops was just  so attention-grabbing not that that's a  bad thing though in fact rather  unexpectedly we even had a bit of a  sit-down chat with cyclops san where he  unveiled an interesting counter  philosophy the whole concept that curses  are actually humanity's purest form and  what inhabits this world as we speak  of these lying facades of humankind and  i really like that as an antagonistic  motivating thought much better than your  classic qualcomm more powerful than you  so this world should be mine kind of  crap in jiu jitsu guy said it actually  seems like there's more of a core belief  to be grappled with because as far as  i'm aware the cyclops  well he's not exactly wrong is he the  curses aren't aberrations of the world  they're more of just  natural evolution are they not and i  don't know but are we eventually going  to have to grapple with the idea that  perhaps curses have just as much right  to exist  as the humans that spawn them no idea  but i do like that these sorts of ideas  are being brought up at such an early  stage it makes me much more intrigued to  see more of these antagonists as soon as  possible please  and similarly we have also expanded into  a batch of new students one of which  is the aforementioned panda and in all  seriousness pandas are by far my  favorite animal so this is very welcome  news  i really don't care how we're talking  panda exists or why it might be a mighty  curse sorcerer none of it matters all i  know is that jujutsu kaisen has gone  from like a seven to a ten all due to  panda propaganda and two other students  were also introduced i don't have any  strong comment on them at this time but  they did also seem to come with the  reminder that jude kaisen is for all of  its cursed horror also  a high school series with an upcoming  enter high event against  another jujutsu school a jujutsu battle  where the only rule  